Using Flower
Pendant ships as one Flower AgentApp, so you type a music prompt into flwr chat and the whole band runs inside Flower. I ran this end to end on 2026-09-30 with Flower 1.39.0, offline provider: it made an 8-bar funk song in 7 calls.

What Flower does here. Flower runs the app, carries your chat prompt to it, and streams progress back. With the OpenAI provider, it also proxies model calls so your key stays on the SuperLink. It does not spread the musicians across machines: all agents run inside the one AgentApp (pendant_flower/agent_app.py), which calls the same run() as the command line.

Run it offline (no API key)
Clone into a folder without an underscore. flwr build rejects pendant_music, because app names allow only letters, digits and hyphens.

git clone -b codex/complete-pendant https://github.com/Pranjal101Shrivastava/pendant_music pendant
cd pendant
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements-flower.txt      # Pendant + flwr 1.39.x
Edit [tool.flwr.app.config] in pyproject.toml. Use an absolute output-dir, because the app runs in its own process:

provider = "offline"
mode = "autonomous"
bars = 8
output-dir = "/absolute/path/to/pendant/outputs/flower"
Check that the bundle builds: flwr build should print Successfully built local.pendant.0-2-0.<hash>.fab.

Start chat against the local SuperLink. Without the variable, flwr chat tried Flower's hosted SuperLink (api.flower.ai) in my test and failed:

FLWR_CHAT_SUPERLINK=local flwr chat
In the chat, type /load ., wait for Loaded @local/pendant, then type a prompt such as upbeat funk, 110 BPM.

The reply names the song and the folder. Each run gets its own random subfolder: <output-dir>/<run id>/<prompt>/song.mid, plus song.json and report.json. Leave with /quit.

After the reply, Flower may print Error: Chat run ended before the agent response completed. In my run the song was already written, so the files are fine. After changing code or config, type /load . again. Don't use flwr run: on 1.39 it leaves out the prompt the SuperLink requires.

Run it with OpenAI models
Set provider = "openai" in pyproject.toml (optionally model = "...").

Start your own SuperLink with the OpenAI endpoint and key:

export FLWR_MODEL_API_ENDPOINT=https://api.openai.com/v1/responses
export FLWR_MODEL_API_KEY="$OPENAI_API_KEY"
flower-superlink --insecure --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8000 --fleet-api-address 127.0.0.1:9092
Add the connection to ~/.flwr/config.toml (or $FLWR_HOME/config.toml):

[superlink.pendant]
address = "127.0.0.1:8000"
insecure = true
In a second terminal with the venv active: FLWR_CHAT_SUPERLINK=pendant flwr chat, then /load . and your prompt.

The app never sees your OpenAI key. Flower gives it FLWR_RUNTIME_BASE_URL and FLWR_RUNTIME_API_KEY, and the SuperLink forwards requests to OpenAI. PENDANT_MODEL_<AGENT> still overrides one agent's model on a local runtime. --insecure is for your own machine only. This path passed against a mock OpenAI server in the smoke test, but has not been tried with a real OpenAI account.

